  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {"@type":"Question","name":"Why is fall the best time for CO2 laser and other procedures?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"UV damage is the single biggest risk factor for post-procedure hyperpigmentation, and ablative treatments like CO2 laser make skin especially UV-sensitive for weeks after. In peak summer, the risk of a darkened patch forming where the laser hit is high. From October through December, that risk drops significantly. Dermatologists and plastic surgeons know this, and so do the women who have been through a few annual cycles. Appointments in those months fill up early."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between CO2 laser, Sculptra, and microneedling?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"CO2 fractional laser creates controlled micro-wounds to trigger a large collagen remodeling response. It is the most aggressive of the three, with the longest downtime and the most visible result. Sculptra is a biostimulator injected into the deeper layers of the face. It prompts your body to rebuild its own collagen over months. Microneedling creates smaller micro-wounds using tiny needles. It is the gentlest of the three, with the shortest downtime and the most gradual result. CO2 resurfaces. Sculptra restores structure. Microneedling supports and maintains."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"How much do CO2 laser, Sculptra, and microneedling cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"CO2 fractional laser runs $1,500 to $3,500 per session depending on the device and the depth of treatment. Most people need one session per year. Sculptra runs about $800 to $1,200 per vial, and most faces need two to three vials over a protocol of two to three sessions. Microneedling at a medical office runs $300 to $600 per session, with most protocols calling for three to six sessions. All three are investments. Budget for the full protocol and the recovery products, not just the first session."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"How long is the recovery for CO2 laser?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Plan for one full week of visible recovery after CO2 fractional laser. Days one to three involve redness, swelling, and oozing. Days four to seven involve peeling and tight skin. From day eight through about three weeks, the skin looks pink and sensitive. Strict sun protection and avoidance of actives like retinoids is critical through the full healing window. Full collagen remodeling results peak at three to six months, not at week two."}},
      {"@type":"Question","name":"Can I do CO2 laser and Sculptra in the same session?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Do not stack CO2 and Sculptra at the same appointment. Allow CO2 to heal fully, which takes four to six weeks, before adding Sculptra. Or do Sculptra first and wait three months for the collagen response to begin before scheduling CO2. Ask your provider which sequence makes sense for your situation. Both treatments stimulate collagen through different mechanisms, and stacking them at once can overwhelm the healing response and increase complications."}}
    ]
  }
  </script>

