<section class="bottom-line">
  <div class="bottom-line-inner">
    <div class="bottom-line-label">Bottom Line</div>
    <h2>Pick the treatment that answers your actual question.</h2>
    <p>CO2 is the right answer for texture, tone, and laxity, and fall is the only safe window to book it. Sculptra is the right answer for volume loss and structural change, especially if you are on a GLP-1 or deep in perimenopause. Microneedling is the right answer for a lower-commitment entry or ongoing maintenance between bigger treatments. The three are not interchangeable. Book the one that answers your question, do not stack them at the same session, and lock in the daily skincare routine that holds the result. If you are weighing CO2 or Sculptra for the first time, book the consult now. Good providers are already filling up for the fall window.</p>
  </div>
</section>

